{"id":"chatcmpl-f44181fb-fd2c-4d38-b402-9b55276d6478","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249476,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation, where conflicting outputs between specialized tools are resolved through a verification step before finalizing. The key insight is that orientation markers (like 'L' markers) indicate projection orientation, not anatomical laterality, and must be interpreted carefully. The pattern generalizes to any visual QA task where multiple models may disagree and spatial orientation cues can mislead.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When multiple independent visual models disagree on a finding, invoke a verification step to adjudicate before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Distinguish orientation/projection markers from anatomical laterality cues—markers indicate view orientation, not device side.\",\n    \"Use a domain-specialist tool first for targeted visual analysis, then cross-validate with a general-purpose model to catch errors.\",\n    \"When a tool reports absence while another reports presence, treat the discrepancy as a signal to escalate rather than defaulting to either output.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Route laterality/presence questions to a specialist model first, then confirm with a second model; always interpret orientation markers as view indicators, not anatomical labels.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus tasks\": \"Design workflows with an explicit conflict-resolution step; do not average or default—use a verifier to adjudicate disagreements.\",\n    \"Spatial reasoning with markers\": \"Separate marker semantics (projection orientation) from target semantics (anatomical side) before drawing conclusions.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether any orientation marker (e.g., 'L') refers to view projection rather than anatomical laterality before assigning a side.\",\n    \"If tool outputs conflict on presence/laterality, trigger verification and document the resolution rationale before answering.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":565,"total_tokens":939,"completion_tokens":374,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":565},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":374}}}